Before Creating Autopsy Case Create On Empty Folder Give Name Email Analysis
Step 1: Open Autopsy
Select: Create New Case

Step 2: Create Case
Enter:
Case Name:     Exp7
Base Directory: Email Analysis Saved Folder
Case Number:   7
Examiner:Student
Click Finish.

Step 3: Select Host
If Autopsy asks for the host, select:
Generate new host name based on data source name
Click Next.

Step 4: Add Evidence
Add Data Source
Select:
Disk Image or VM File
Click Next.

Step 5: Select E01 Image
Select:
C:\Forensic_Images\EmailEvidence.E01
Click Next.

Step 6: Processing
If your Autopsy version displays ingest/processing options, enable useful modules such as:
File Type Identification
Keyword Search
If the option does not appear, continue with the default processing.
Click next and finish.

Step 7: Examine Email Messages
In the left panel, open:
Data Artifacts
       ↓
E-Mail Messages
In your case, you may see:
E-Mail Messages (4)
Click it.

Step 8: Examine Email Headers
Select an email and examine:
From
To
Subject
Date/Time
Message-ID
Record the information.

Step 9: Examine Attachment
Open the email containing an attachment.
Check:
Attachment name
Attachment type
Attachment contents/metadata

Step 10: Examine Suspicious Email
Open the suspicious email.
Check for:
Suspicious sender
Urgent request
Password request
Account verification
Suspicious links
Suspicious attachment

Step 11: Examine Incomplete Email
Open the incomplete email.
Check which header fields are available and which are missing.

Step 12: Keyword Search
Use Keyword Search.
Search for:
urgent
password
verification
account
confidential
Record the matching results.

Step 13: Generate Report
Use:
Generate Report
Select an available format such as:
HTML
PDF
CSV
